title the jail had no word for codex
prompt Update the tree to the latest after a force push from the macOS session; set up the NixOS config for installing ChatGPT Codex for Linux, instruct the nixos-rebuild outside the jail if needed, prove the config builds cleanly, then send; and prepare for the newly assigned Dream Codex in ai-jail on the Vultr pier holding the systems core -- Caravan, Tally, the microkernel road, the constellation table.
think ListAgents named no peer, so this lap carries no %291 shadow. The sync came first and it was not the force-push it looked like: HEAD was a strict ancestor of xy/main, 0 ahead and 2 behind, so nothing was lost. What was at risk sat in the working tree -- a complete uncommitted round with its session log already written, the %292 exec-bit work. Committing it before rebasing was the move that preserved it; discarding to a clean ff would have thrown away a finished lap.
think The tree also carried 1,326 untracked .tpr files from an interrupted tools/fixtures/tool_path_repoint_scan.sh. I checked rather than assumed: 1,325 byte-identical to their originals and one, tools/cr/crypto_monocypher_xaead_parity_witness.rish.tpr, at zero bytes. That last one matters -- the script's apply path is cat "$f.tpr" > "$f", so an --apply run over that leftover would have truncated a live 67-line witness to nothing. The sweep only runs at the end, so any interruption litters and arms that trap. Deleted all 1,326; the underlying fragility is named here rather than repaired, being a lane of its own.
think Two conflicts on the rebase, both in files the two hands had each rewritten. session-logs/README.md was ordering only. construction/ITINERARY.md was the Now block, where upstream's is authoritative -- it carries the role swap this round exists to serve. Measurement decided it: upstream's card reads exactly 24,576 bytes against a bound of 24,576, so there was no room for a merge of both and any addition had to be paid for by a cut. Took upstream whole and rewrote the block once, at the close, where the round's own facts could be spent against that budget deliberately.
think The provisioning question had a real fork and I measured before choosing. codex IS in the locked nixpkgs at 0.133.0, and my first cache probe read 404, which would have made a source build of a large Rust workspace the only nixpkgs road on a 4-core 8 GB pier. That probe was wrong -- a nix build --dry-run said "will be fetched, 96.2 MiB", so 0.133.0 installs from cache with nothing compiled. Correcting that before recommending changed the question from necessity to preference, and it went to Keaton, who took the overlay.
think Then the finding the round actually turned on, and it was not in the plan. Dream's launcher prints ./tools/ag/agent-jail.sh env CODEX_HOME=... codex exec on four separate lines, and agent-jail.sh dispatches its first non-flag argument through a case with three arms -- claude, cursor-agent, agent. The first argument is env. I ran it rather than reading it: unknown command: env, exit 2. The star's whole seat could not start, and everything around it was correct -- the gitignore entry, the state directory, the charter, the sandbox flag. A launcher that prints a recipe proves its own printing, which is why it read GREEN the whole time.
think The repair follows the jail's own pattern rather than the launcher's. Mapping .dream-state/codex-home onto ~/.codex the way the three existing state maps work makes the CODEX_HOME dance unnecessary, so the seat's invocation gets shorter as it gets correct. Proven three ways on metal: the unknown-command refusal still bites, the codex arm with no binary prints a named refusal carrying the switch command, and the codex arm with the binary on PATH emits a dry-run bwrap plan with the bind and the landlock-rw path both present.
think agent_jail_witness went RED and I checked whether it was mine before believing it. git stash, re-run, identical failure -- bwrap: Failed to make / slave, which is nested bubblewrap refusing inside ai-jail. A machine limit, not a tree defect, exactly the distinction Dream's seat prompt names. The two legs that can run inside the jail both PASS with the new map in place, including the dry-run map check.
think Upstream moved a second time at the push, and the collision was the interesting kind. The shed lane
 had booked its own %292 at 20260827.162143 -- a different red entirely, four unrostered chapter witnesses
 that a rename and an ASCII sweep had left behind. Two hands numbered the same row from two hosts, which is
 %291's one-checkout question wearing the ledger's clothes. The recital already seats the answer: the push to
 xy is the allocation, so upstream's number stands and the later ones move. Rebased rather than forced, three
 times, taking upstream's rows whole each time and re-seating mine -- %292-%294 to %294-%296. The pin could not
 hold two lanes' rounds at once, so %289, %290, and %292 folded onto shelves by reds_fold.sh. A born-on-shelf row
 was the shorter road and I tried it first; the monotone scan refused it, correctly, and the fold is what the
 ledger's own tool is for.
obs Measurement beat memory twice, and once it corrected me. The cache 404 nearly became a recommendation built on a wrong fact; the dry-run was cheap and said otherwise. And the seat's defect was invisible to reading and obvious to running -- three files were written with care about Codex and the refusal lived in a fourth that the round's shape never asked anyone to open.
obs Scope held on the two open gates. %291's one-tree-per-star and %293's host-tier shape both stayed named and untaken, and the width ratchet in glow/rune_shape.rye stayed measured and waiting. The REDS pin had 258 bytes against a row wanting ten times that, so %289 and %290 folded onto a shelf to make room and the codex row was born on one. Upstream then booked its own %292 from the shed lane mid-round, and its own %293 an hour later, so all three of this round's rows re-seated %292-%294 to %294-%296 across two rebases -- the push to xy is the allocation, fourth and fifth firings of that door.
loom sync behind=2 ahead=0 conflicts=2 tpr_deleted=1326 tpr_zero_byte=1
