loom reds pin_bytes=22850 bound=24576 spine=1..296 gaps=0 rows_folded=3 renumbered=3 renumber_passes=2
file nixos/configuration.nix the third agent-CLI overlay -- codex 0.150.1, prebuilt static musl, replacing the source-built derivation
file nixos/rebuild-outer.sh the switch witnesses codex --version beside perl, python3, and claude
file tools/ag/agent-jail.sh the fourth arm: codex resolved, refused by name when absent, state mapped onto ~/.codex
file tools/l/launch-dream-dual-chapter.rish all four printed lines drop the CODEX_HOME dance; provisioning names the switch
file construction/archive/REDS-the-jail-that-had-no-word-for-codex-rows-296.md %296 born on a shelf; booked %294 and re-seated twice as upstream published %292 then %293
file construction/archive/REDS-fold-recital.md two recital rows -- the %289-%290 and %292 folds that made room, and where %296 was born
file construction/REDS.md %289-%290 and %292 folded off, the headline regenerated to the measured spine, 1..296
file construction/ITINERARY.md the Now block rewritten inside the 24,576 budget; the nib names the parent
recommend check-in (Keaton) -- the switch is yours and runs outside the jail: bash /home/keeper/grain/nixos/rebuild-outer.sh, then ./tools/ag/agent-jail.sh codex login once. Everything up to that line is proven on metal here. After it lands, Dream opens core-first: Caravan and Tally green, then the constellation table. Gated and unchanged: %291's one-tree-per-star, %293's host-tier shape, the 59 gate fixtures, and the width ratchet in glow/rune_shape.rye.
